  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A satellite of mass <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"m\"></span> orbits a planet of mass <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"M\"></span> and radius <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"R\"></span>, initially at a distance <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"R\"></span> from the surface of the planet. During its orbit, the satellite collides with the gas atoms in the upper atmosphere of the planet and as a result, its orbital radius changes by <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{R}{2}\"></span>.</p>\n<p>What is the total energy of the satellite after this change?</p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"-\\frac{GMm}{R}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"-\\frac{GMm}{2R}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"-\\frac{GMm}{3R}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"-\\frac{GMm}{5R}\"></span></li>\n</ol>"
  },
